  "description": "DAFHAV crystallizes in the hexagonal crystal system with space group P 63/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C132 H86 Dy11 N30 O41 1+,40(H2 O1),H1 O1 1-,7(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1I (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1K (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1J (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2I (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.564-3.992 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.65-118.17°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy11(OH)11(phendox)6(phenda)3(OAc)3](OH)·40H2O·7MeOH (C139H195Dy11N30O89). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 11 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 11 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
